// Regression test (OVH-003, docs/planning/OVERHAUL_REMAINING_WORK.md):
// indexing a raw pointer-typed base (`someList.data[i]`, where `data: T*`)
// must be rejected outside `unsafe { }`/a raw-pointer-capability module,
// exactly like field/member access through one already is. Before this
// fix, TypeChecker::visitArrayAccess() never called checkUnsafeGate() at
// all -- `l.data[100000] = 42;` compiled with no `unsafe { }` and no
// capability declared anywhere in this file, an out-of-bounds write
// reachable from ordinary safe code (F-PTR-1's "raw pointers are
// FFI-only" promise silently didn't apply to indexing). See
// raw_pointer_index_inside_unsafe_ok.tr for the corresponding passing
// case, and list_get_set_generic.tr for the safe, bounds-checked
// replacement (`List<T>.get()`/`.set()`) this file's uses should migrate
// to instead of reaching for `unsafe { }`.

import list::List;

fn main(): int {
    mut l: List<int> = List::default();
    l.push(1);
    l.data[100000] = 42;
    return 0;
}
